    "SQLBase Database File",
    "3.6",
    "Database file created by SQLBase, an embedded database solution for business applications; stores structured data and tracks changes to the data in a .log file; often used for storing data for small desktop programs or mobile applications. Gupta Technologies, the original developers of SQLBase, renamed to Centura Software in the 1990s. In 2006, Centura Software was acquired by Unify Corporation. Windows Gupta SQLBase. Linux Gupta SQLBase. Three-dimensional mesh file created by GAMBIT, a modeling program often used with the FLUENT computational fluid dynamics (CFD) program; stores the 3D geometry of an object used in fluid flow calculations; can be used for studying the flow of water and air around structures. Windows GAMBIT. Linux GAMBIT.",
