    "Access Runtime Application",
    "3.3",
    "Locked-down database file created by the Microsoft Access relational database software; stores an.ACCDB database, except with the extension renamed to .accdr; allows the database to be opened and run in a read-only mode so that no changes are made to the database. If you want to run an ACCDB database in read-only mode, rename the file extension to .accdr and then open it. To restore the database to its original read-write format, rename the extension back to .accdb.. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
