    ["database_files",
    ".ABCDDB",
    "Apple Address Book Contact List ",
    "3.3",
    "File created by Address Book, a contact organization application; contains a contact list, in SQLite database format, of all the contacts stored within the Address Book application; regenerated when the Address Book application is opened; not meant to be manually opened. The ABCDDB file can be found in the following directory: UserHome(Home Icon) > Library > Application Support > AddressBook NOTE: OS X Mountain Lion replaced the Address Book application with the Contacts application. AddressBook-v22.abcddb - If your Address Book contacts arent displaying correctly, quit the application, move this file from the AddressBook folder to your desktop, and start up the Address Book application again. Mac Apple Contacts Included with OS.",
    "Mac Apple Contacts Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".REALM",
    "Realm Database",
    "3.3",
    "A REALM file is a database created using MongoDB Realm, an open-source database management system. It contains data used by one or more applications, organized as a series of types and objects. You can open REALM files and view the data they contain in MongoDB Realm Studio. REALM file open in MongoDB Realm Studio 11 Realm is a database management system that developers can use to allow their apps to create and access databases. These databases contain a variety of app-related information, organized as types and objects. For example, an app that tracks a users online purchases may contain information about the products the user purchased, when the user purchased them, how much the user paid, and so on. Each category (e.g. Product Name) is saved as a database type, while each entry in each category (e.g. Pampers Diapers 204 Pack) is saved as a database object. The databases Realm creates are saved as REALM files. REALM files are primarily binary files, which are not meant to be opened outside of MongoDB Realm Studio. Apps that use Realm save their REALM databases in a variety of locations, depending on the apps platform. For example, on macOS and iOS, many Realm-enabled apps save REALM files to a sub-directory within their Documents directory. On Android devices, you can use the command adb pull /data/data/<packagename>/files/ to retrieve an apps REALM database. How do I convert a CSV file to a REALM file? Developers may want to convert an existing database into a Realm database, so they can use that database with their Realm-enabled application. To do so, developers can save their existing database as a.CSV file and then use MongoDB Realm Studio to convert the CSV file to a REALM file. To convert a CSV file to a REALM file, open Realm Studio and select File → Create Realm from → CSV. You can open a REALM file in MongoDB Realm Studio (cross-platform). To do so, open Realm Studio, select the Open Realm file button, and then navigate to and open your REALM file. The data your REALM file contains will appear in Realm Studio. Windows MongoDB Realm Studio. Mac MongoDB Realm Studio. Linux MongoDB Realm StudioFree.",
    "Windows MongoDB Realm Studio. Mac MongoDB Realm Studio. Linux MongoDB Realm Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".FMP12",
    "FileMaker Pro 12 Database",
    "3.2",
    "Database file created by FileMaker Pro 12, a personal and business database development program; stores the database structure (tables and fields) and the records that fill the tables; may also include custom forms, reports, and other database objects; can include a custom theme for personalizing the interface. FileMaker Pro databases can be used for storing contacts, business inventory, project data, invoices, and other information. Databases may be shared with team members via the Web or by using iPhone and iPad devices with the FileMaker Go app installed. NOTE: The FMP12 format is new with FileMaker Pro 12. FileMaker Pro 7-11 use the.FP7 extension. Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced. Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced. iOS FileMaker Go 19Free.",
    "Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced. Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced. iOS FileMaker Go 19.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".MAF",
    "Microsoft Access Form",
    "3.2",
    "An MAF file is a form created by Microsoft Access, a relational database management system (RDBMS). It contains formatted fields used to enter data into or retrieve data from an.ACCDB database. MAF files are created using Microsoft Accesss Form tool. To allow database managers to more easily enter data into or retrieve data from a Microsoft Access database, the program allows managers to create and link forms with database tables. To create a form, managers select the table for which they want to create a form, select Create from Microsoft Accesss menu bar, and then select Form. Access then creates a form that contains fields linked to the tables columns. Each Microsoft Access form is saved as an MAF file. You can open an MAF file in Microsoft Access to edit the forms fields and appearance, using Accesss Form Layout Tools. You can also use a form to search for or enter data into a database, provided you have access to that database. Forms may include subforms, which show information from related tables. For example, a form used to search for or add customers to a database may include a subform that shows information about customers orders, which is stored in a related table. How do I set a Microsoft Access form (MAF file) as a databases default form? After you finish creating a Microsoft Access form, you may want to set that form as your databases default form. This will cause the form to appear automatically each time you open the database. To set a form as a databases default form: Select File → Options. Select Current Database. From the Display Form list, select the form you want to use as your databases default form. Select OK. You can open an MAF file in Microsoft Access (Windows). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar, and then navigate to and open your MAF file. You can then use the form to enter data into or retrieve data from the table it is linked with, or you can edit the form using Microsoft Accesss Form Design Tools. To access Accesss Form Design Tools, select the View button found in Accesss toolbar, and then select Layout view or Design view. Windows Microsoft Access 365. Text file created in the Mutation Annotation Format (MAF), a file format used to capture mutations in cells; saves cell and genome information using tab-delimited text; used in cancer studies for capturing somatic mutations and single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNPs). The MAF format is maintained by the National Cancer Institute and the National Human Genome Research Institute (NHGRI) under a project named The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA). The format is primarily used by custom research analysis software applications. However, MAF files can be viewed with any text editor. NOTE: The MAF format has undergone several revisions. Version 2.2 supports 32 different tab-delimited columns. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Microsoft WordPad Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "Windows Microsoft Access 365. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Microsoft WordPad Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DB-SHM",
    "SQLite Database Shared Memory File",
    "3.2",
    "Temporary file created by SQLite, a compact database program often embedded into mobile and desktop applications; used by the database for shared memory storage and is automatically created and maintained by SQLite; not meant to be opened manually. DB-SHM files are also created with.DB-WAL files. Both files are created as extra temporary files for a database and do not need to be copied with the original database to preserve the data. Since SQLite is a popular technology, you may see these files in an application data directory. NOTE: A database file mydb.db may have mydb.db-shm and mydb.db-wal temporary files. Windows SQLite. Mac SQLite. Linux SQLiteFree.",
    "Windows SQLite. Mac SQLite. Linux SQLite.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".PDB",
    "Palm Desktop Database File",
    "3.2",
    "A PDB file is a database file used by various applications, including Pegasus, Quicken, Microsoft Visual Studio, and Palm Pilot software. It stores data in a structured format and is typically installed with the corresponding application. PDB files used by different programs are usually saved in different proprietary formats, meaning they can be opened only by the program they were installed with. For example, Microsoft Visual Studio will not recognize an Intuit Quicken PDB file. Visual Studio uses PDB files to store debugging information about a program, including symbol information, which is too large to be stored in the program itself. The symbol information consists of a list of all symbols in a program module with addresses, the name of the file, and the line the symbol was declared on. You can use Microsoft Visual Studio (Windows) to load information from a PDB file created by that program. This allows you to debug the program the file is associated with. You can also use Microsofts CVDump program (Windows) to read the information a Visual Studio PDB file contains. Windows Intuit Quicken. Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Microsoft CVDump. Mac Intuit Quicken. Data file created in the Protein Data Bank (PDB) format; stores 3D coordinates specifying the structure of atoms within a protein or other chemical compound; used as a standard format for studying protein structures; also used by the Research Collaboratory for Structural Bioinformatics (RCSB) for studying biological macromolecules. Many Protein Data Bank files are made available through the Worldwide Protein Data Bank (wwPDB), an organization that archives macromolecules and freely distributes them. NOTE: PDB files are often viewed within a Java applet that uses Jmol, an open source molecule visualization package. PDB files are also supported by some molecular viewing browser plugins. Windows Avogadro. Jmol. RasMol. Microsoft Internet Explorer with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet. Agile Molecule Abalone —  (Discontinued). Agile Molecule Ascalaph —  (Discontinued). Mac Avogadro. Jmol. Apple Safari with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet Included with OS. Linux Avogadro. Jmol. RasMol. Mozilla Firefox with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet. Web Animated PhysicsFree. Movie project file created and used by Demo Builder, a program used to create tutorials, presentations, and demonstrations to show how software and systems work; contains recorded screen scenes, along with imported video and images. A Demo Builder movie project can be exported to a variety of formats depending on how you want to present your tutorial. Supported formats include Flash, HTML, Windows Media Video, MPEG4, and Word Document. Windows Tanida Demo Builder. Backup of a PowerDesigner database (.PDM) file; includes data saved in the database as well as references to other files; created as a backup in case the main database file needs to be restored. Windows Sybase PowerDesigner. Standard data format used by several different programs on Palm-based PDA devices; may store various types of data, such as eBooks, word processing documents, spreadsheets, databases, maps, and image files. To determine what program created a PDB file, open the file in a text editor. The Type and Creator codes should be located in the header of the file near the top of the document. Windows Palm Desktop. Fictionwise eReader. DC & Co iSilo. XnViewMP. Mac Planamesa NeoOffice. Fictionwise eReader. Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. PorDiBle txt2pdbdoc. XnViewMP. Linux txt2pdbdoc. XnViewMP. Android Fictionwise eReaderFree.",
    "Windows Intuit Quicken. Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Microsoft CVDump. Mac Intuit Quicken. Windows Avogadro. Jmol. RasMol. Microsoft Internet Explorer with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet. Agile Molecule Abalone —  (Discontinued). Agile Molecule Ascalaph —  (Discontinued). Mac Avogadro. Jmol. Apple Safari with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet Included with OS. Linux Avogadro. Jmol. RasMol. Mozilla Firefox with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet. Web Animated Physics. Windows Tanida Demo Builder. Windows Sybase PowerDesigner. Windows Palm Desktop. Fictionwise eReader. DC & Co iSilo. XnViewMP. Mac Planamesa NeoOffice. Fictionwise eReader. Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. PorDiBle txt2pdbdoc. XnViewMP. Linux txt2pdbdoc. XnViewMP. Android Fictionwise eReader.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".VIS",
    "Visual Importer Script",
    "3.1",
    "Script created by Visual Importer, a data conversion application; saves in a plain text format and stores data conversion settings recorded from the softwares wizard walkthrough process; transforms data between source and destination formats when run in the software. VIS scripts save information such as the source data format (plain text, MS Access, MySQL,.CSV, etc.) as well as the destination format. They can also save database connection information and rules for converting data between database records, spreadsheet cells, and plain text. NOTE: VIS files are also referred to as VImp files. Windows DB Software Laboratory Visual Importer. Image information format developed for simulation purposes that includes scenery and maps; used by video games, such as Microsoft Flight Simulator 95 and 98 and other flight simulation programs. VIS files are saved in a text format that may be viewed in a text editor. However, they typically should not be opened or edited by the user. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition.",
    "Windows DB Software Laboratory Visual Importer. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".CAT",
    "Advanced Disk Catalog Database",
    "3.1",
    "File used by the Windows operating system; specifies that a group of files are from a verifiable source; used for security purposes and contains a digital signature, the catalog version, and an effective date; often used for verifying new software update files. Windows catalog files help to suppress multiple trust dialog popups for new software component downloads. Since CAT files can identify a trusted source, the user can choose to Always trust content from the software distributor. Then, future downloads from the software distributor that use a CAT file are trusted and do not require a trust popup window. Windows Microsoft Windows. Contains a catalog of data from various media types including hard drives, network drives, floppy disks, optical discs (DVDs, CDs, etc.), ZIP and JAZ disks, etc.; used for keeping track of information stored within a collection of media. Windows Elcomsoft Advanced Disk Catalog.",
    "Windows Microsoft Windows. Windows Elcomsoft Advanced Disk Catalog.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".QRY",
    "Query File",
    "3.1",
    "Generic query file often containing database queries written in SQL, a language used to insert, update, or delete records from relational databases; sometimes used to run a single query or to run multiple queries in batch; can be executed with products such as MySQL and Microsoft SQL Server. QRY files may also use proprietary formats specific to the software application they are associated with. Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019. MySQL. Mac MySQL. Linux MySQL.",
    "Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019. MySQL. Mac MySQL. Linux MySQL.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ODB",
    "Abaqus Output Database",
    "3.1",
    "An ODB file contains a database created by Apache OpenOffice Base (OOBase), an open-source desktop relational database program. It stores an archive of data files that comprise the database and is formatted according to the OpenDocument standard. ODB files are used to save structured information such as tables and records. ODB file open in Apache OpenOffice Base 4.1.3 OpenDocument databases contain a collection of files and folders that are compressed using Zip compression. They include settings.xml, context.xml, and manifest.xml files, as well as a database folder that contains the following files: properties: stores database settings script: contains table definitions data: contains the current state of the database backup: stores a compressed backup of the last consistent database state log: records changes to the database NOTE: The Organization for the Advancement of Structured Information Standards (OASIS) maintains the OpenDocument standard. You can open an ODB file in OpenOffice Base (cross-platform) or LibreOffice Base (cross-platform). In OpenOffice Base, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar to open your ODB file. You can also decompress your ODB file to manually examine the.XML files and database folder it contains. To do so, rename your ODB file to use the.zip extension and then decompress it with any Zip decompression utility, such as 7-Zip (Windows), Apple Archive Utility (Mac), or B1. Archiver (cross-platform). Windows OpenOffice Base. LibreOffice. 7-Zip. B1. Archiver. Mac OpenOffice Base. Planamesa NeoOffice. LibreOffice. Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. B1. Archiver. Linux OpenOffice Base. LibreOffice. B1. ArchiverFree. An ODB file is an output database created by Abaqus software, a suite of applications that provide finite element analysis (FEA) and computer-aided engineering (CAE) capabilities. It contains a database filled with X-Y data objects organized into two columns (X and Y). Examples of data in an ODB file include load vs. displacement, stress vs. strain, and temperature vs. time of engineering-related simulations. The first version of Abaqus was released in 1978 (formerly ABAQUS) and has since grown into a suite of applications prominent in various commercial and academic mechanical engineering industries. Some industry examples include aerospace and automotive. You can create ODB files to store databases generated from engineering simulations conducted by Abaqus software. After creating the databases, you can open ODB files to view and manipulate their data for visualization and analysis purposes. However, depending on the Abaqus version that created the ODB file, the file may be read-only. To modify a read-only ODB file, you must uncheck the Read Only option near the bottom of the Open Database dialog box when opening the file. You can open an ODB file with the Abaqus suite of applications. To open an ODB file, select File → Open. Abaqus can open ODB files created by previous versions of the software but cannot open ODB files created by later versions. For example, Abaqus 2019 can open ODB files created by version 2017 but not version 2021. Windows Dassault Systemes Abaqus. Linux Dassault Systemes Abaqus. An ODB file contains data extracted from a Windows PC using Oxygen Forensics KeyScout, a component of Oxygen Forensics Detective. The data an ODB file contains may include a users Internet passwords, cookies, history, bookmarks, autofill data, iTunes backups, Wi-Fi hotspot passwords, and operating system artifacts. ODB files can be imported into Oxygen Forensics JetEngine to view the data they contain. Oxygen Forensics Detective is a data extraction and analysis toolset that forensic investigators use to retrieve user data from PCs and mobile devices. Oxygen Forensics KeyScout is a Detective tool that extracts Internet-related data, such as a users passwords, tokens, and browsing history, from Windows PCs. KeyScout can extract data from many applications and web browsers, including WhatsApp Desktop, iCloud, Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, and Internet Explorer. Most of the data KeyScout extracts is saved in ODB files. After saving data in an ODB file, investigators can load and analyze that data in Oxygen Forensics JetEngine, another Forensics Detective tool. You can open an ODB file using Oxygen Forensics JetEngine, which is included with Oxygen Forensics Detective. To do so, open JetEngine and select Backup Import. Then, select and open your ODB file. Windows Oxygen Forensics Detective.",
    "Windows OpenOffice Base. LibreOffice. 7-Zip. B1. Archiver. Mac OpenOffice Base. Planamesa NeoOffice. LibreOffice. Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. B1. Archiver. Linux OpenOffice Base. LibreOffice. B1. Archiver. Windows Dassault Systemes Abaqus. Linux Dassault Systemes Abaqus. Windows Oxygen Forensics Detective.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".TPS",
    "Clarion TopSpeed Data File",
    "3.1",
    "Format used to store data recorded with TiePie Multi Channel software; saves data logged by the program as well as instrument settings for the measurement tools; each measurement is stored in a separate file. Windows TiePie Multi Channel softwareFree. Database format used by Clarion TopScan or TopSpeed; saves data as a flat file, which records one entry per line, with fields separated by spaces or commas; Clarion is often used to create custom database applications. TPS files can be read by Clarion software and by programs that support SoftVelocitys TopSpeed ODBC driver. Windows SoftVelocity Clarion. 3D shape file used by Bryce, a 3D landscape modeling program; contains the shape of a specific type of tree, such as a birch, maple, coconut, or ash tree; commonly used for generating forestry or other background scenery. Mac DAZ 3D Bryce 7 Pro. Windows DAZ 3D Bryce 7 Pro. File created by TexturePacker, a program used for creating sprite sheets and for optimizing images; stores a sprite sheet, which is a canvas arrayed tightly with bitmap images; enables multiple images to be compacted within the same file. TPS files may store different poses for animating a sprite-based character or other object. They are often used for storing textures and other graphics for games. Mac CodenWeb TexturePacker. Windows CodenWeb TexturePacker. Linux CodenWeb TexturePacker.",
    "Windows TiePie Multi Channel software. Windows SoftVelocity Clarion. Mac DAZ 3D Bryce 7 Pro. Windows DAZ 3D Bryce 7 Pro. Mac CodenWeb TexturePacker. Windows CodenWeb TexturePacker. Linux CodenWeb TexturePacker.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DCX",
    "FoxPro Database Index",
    "3.0",
    "Multi-page image file created by various image programs; contains a small header that identifies the DCX file followed by a sequence of.PCX files; commonly used to create digital fax files. The DCX file format was originally developed by Zsoft. Web File Helper. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. XnViewMP. IrfanView. CoolUtils Total Image Converter. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. XnViewMPFree. Index used by a FoxPro database, which improves the efficiency of searching and sorting items in the database. Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Fax format used by ACCPAC FAXserve, a program that can send, receive, and broadcast faxes from a computer; saves images and text in a digital format that is viewable by multiple fax programs. Windows ACCPAC FAXserve GraphicRegion Able Fax Tif View SFaxTools Studio FaxSee Pro or Smart FaxSee.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. XnViewMP. IrfanView. CoolUtils Total Image Converter. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. XnViewMP. Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Windows ACCPAC FAXserve GraphicRegion Able Fax Tif View SFaxTools Studio FaxSee Pro or Smart FaxSee.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DBV",
    "Database Variable Field",
    "3.0",
    "Defines database fields of variable length; can be used to designate the size of text and binary (BLOB data type) fields; referenced by an xBase-compatible database (.DBF) file with the same name. Windows dBase. multisoft FlagShip. Clipper.",
    "Windows dBase. multisoft FlagShip. Clipper.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".SAS7BDAT",
    "SAS Dataset File",
    "3.0",
    "A SAS7BDAT file is a database storage file created by Statistical Analysis System (SAS) software. It contains a binary encoded dataset used for advanced analytics, business intelligence, data management, predictive analytics, and more. SAS is a statistical software suite that data analysts use to manage and analyze data. It allows analysts to create statistical models, perform multivariate analysis, graph and present data, and engage in predictive analytics. In SAS version 7, the suite began saving users datasets as SAS7BDAT files. These files are binary database files that contain a header and data pages. The header lists the databases ID, name, contents, and other metadata. The data pages contain subheaders that include additional metadata, as well as the packed binary data that represents the databases dataset. NOTE: SAS7BDAT files created on different platforms use slightly different file formats. However, you can use any SAS7BDAT file with any platforms version of SAS. SAS7BDAT files are not meant to be opened. Instead, they are meant to be imported into SAS (Windows, Linux) via the applications libname command. For example, to access a SAS7BDAT file located at C:/​Documents/​example.sas7bdat, you would enter libname examplerefname C:/Documents/example.sas7bdat in your SAS session. You could then access the dataset by referring to it as examplerefname. For more detailed instructions, refer to SASs official documentation. Windows SAS Institute SAS. sas7bdat.py. Mac sas7bdat.py. Linux SAS Institute SAS. sas7bdat.pyFree.",
    "Windows SAS Institute SAS. sas7bdat.py. Mac sas7bdat.py. Linux SAS Institute SAS. sas7bdat.py.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DB2",
    "dBASE II Database",
    "3.0",
    "Video information file generated by a Samsung CCTV recording system; contains information about a corresponding.BU video file. DB2 files are saved with BU files in the same directory and have the same filename, expect for the extension. For example, a video recording may generate the files 12300000.bu and 12300000.db2. These files should not be separated since they are both read by Samsung video recording software. Windows Samsung SmartViewer. Database file created by dBASE II, an older version of dBASE database application development software; similar to dBASE 1 databases, but may support additional data types; not commonly used, since recent versions of dBASE use the.DBF format. NOTE: DB2 files created by dBASE shouldnt be confused with IBM DB2 database software. Windows dBase.",
    "Windows Samsung SmartViewer. Windows dBase.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ADE",
    "Access Project Extension",
    "3.0",
    "Database project file created by Microsoft Access, a desktop database program; contains all data saved in a.ADP project, except the modules written in the Visual Basic for Applications (VBA) programming language are compiled and the source code is removed. ADE files are also compressed so that they reduce the file size and optimize performance in Access. Even with the file compression and source code compilation, all database components in an ADE file behave in the same manner as the existing ADP project file. NOTE: ADE projects help protect proprietary VBA source code by disallowing the original source code to be viewed or edited. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DBT",
    "Database Text File",
    "3.0",
    "Text file used for memo fields of dBASE and other xBase database programs. Windows dBase. Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Swiftpage Act!. Any text editor.",
    "Windows dBase. Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Swiftpage Act!. Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".MDBHTML",
    "Microsoft Access Database HTML File",
    "3.0",
    "HTML version of database created by Microsoft Access, a desktop database application; contains HTML source code generated from the database schema and populated data; used for viewing a database in an HTML format. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".PNZ",
    "Panorama Database Set",
    "3.0",
    "File created by Panorama, a fast database and spreadsheet program; saves references to database files (.PAN files) but does not store the actual databases themselves; enables multiple databases to be opened at once. Windows ProVUE Development Panorama. Mac ProVUE Development Panorama.",
    "Windows ProVUE Development Panorama. Mac ProVUE Development Panorama.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".RCTD",
    "RabbitCT Dataset",
    "3.0",
    "Dataset used by RabbitCTRunner, an open platform for benchmarking 3D cone-beam reconstruction algorithms; contains a preprocessed C-arm CT collection of data from a rabbit; accessed by RabbitCTRunner, which performs the benchmark and evaluation of the data. RabbitCTRunner uses the RCTD file to reconstruct the benchmark. This process consists of three steps: Download RabbitCTRunner and the RCTD Dataset from the website (the link is located below under the Windows, Mac, and Linux programs). Download a precompiled back projection module, e.g., LolaBunny, or implement your own backprojection module. Execute RabbitCTRunner from the command line. This will produce a volume file and an encoded result file that can be uploaded to the RabbitCT servers. NOTE: The RCTD file can be downloaded from the same page that the RabbitCTRunner application is downloaded from. Mac RabbitCTRunner. Windows RabbitCTRunner. Linux RabbitCTRunnerFree.",
    "Mac RabbitCTRunner. Windows RabbitCTRunner. Linux RabbitCTRunner.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".SDY",
    "StarMoney User Database File",
    "3.0",
    "An SDY file is a database file created by the Windows version of Star Finanz StarMoney, an online banking application. It contains data entered by a user, such as banking account information and transactions. SDY files are accompanied by.SDX database files, which make up the other part of the database. Star Finanz is a German-based company. It develops several variations of StarMoney, which include personal and business versions, to manage multiple financial accounts. The software creates SDY and SDX files to store all of the data entered by the user. The SDY and SDX database files for the Windows desktop version of StarMoney are located in the following directory (beginning with StarMoney 7.0): C:/​ProgramData/​StarMoney [version]/​Profile The ProgramData folder is hidden by default. You can set hidden files and folders to be shown in the Windows File Explorer utility by following our Windows 8 and Windows 10 video tutorials. SDY files are not meant to be opened. Instead, the Windows version of Star Finanz StarMoney references the files to load the information stored in the files. Windows Star Finanz StarMoney.",
    "Windows Star Finanz StarMoney.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".CMA",
    "TM1 Exported Cube File",
    "3.0",
    "Activity file created and used by Coach, a Dutch computer modeling program that allows users to make dynamic models; stores a measurement or control activity with all the elements that appear in the document, such as pictures, videos, and text; stored in Coach project folders. CMA activity files and.CMR results files contain similar data except activity files only contain the activity. Results files contain the results of a students work in the activity file. NOTE: Coach is a program designed for students between the ages of 8 and 20. It is typically used in schools because of its teaching tools. Windows CMA Coach. Database file exported by Cognos TM1 (formerly Applix TM1), a strategic business planning application; saved in a plain text, comma-delimited format; contains data for a cube, which is a multi-dimensional database containing business intelligence information. CMA files allow users to export data for use in other applications such as spreadsheet programs. Windows IBM Cognos TM1 —  (Discontinued). Trial. Developer library created for use with the OCaml programming language; contains a collection of functions that can be invoked in OCaml programs; often referenced within OCaml source code files (.ML) and can be loaded with the #load directive. Windows OCaml. Mac OCaml. Linux OCamlFree.",
    "Windows CMA Coach. Windows IBM Cognos TM1 —  (Discontinued). Trial. Windows OCaml. Mac OCaml. Linux OCaml.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".EPIM",
    "EssentialPIM Database File",
    "3.0",
    "File used by EssentialPIM, a personal information manager; stores your personal data, such as added tasks, notes, contacts, passwords, calendar items, and appointments. To create an EPIM file, select File → New → EPIM Data File. EPIM files are located in the following directory: C:/​Users/​kellenbloom/​AppData/​Roaming/​EssentialPIM Pro/​. Windows Astonsoft EssentialPIM. iOS Astonsoft EssentialPIM. Android Astonsoft EssentialPIM.",
    "Windows Astonsoft EssentialPIM. iOS Astonsoft EssentialPIM. Android Astonsoft EssentialPIM.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".TSD",
    "Tamino Schema",
    "3.0",
    "A TSD file is a schema saved in the Tamino Schema format. It contains a list of elements that a Tamino XML Server document may contain. TSD files may contain standard XML elements and Tamino-specific elements. Tamino Schema Editor is a GUI-based application that Tamino XML Server users can use to create and edit Tamino Schemas. The schemas users create in the Tamino Schema Editor are saved as TSD files. Each TSD file is an XML file that may contain additional, Tamino-specific elements. These Tamino-specific elements begin with the tag tsd:. For example, each TSD file typically includes a tsd:schemaInfo name = name element, which specifies the schemas name. After a user finishes editing their TSD file, they can import it into Tamino X-Plorer to define a Tamino XML Server database. TSD files are meant to be opened and edited in Tamino Schema Editor (Windows, Linux). The program contains helpful editing tools that allow users to easily manage and edit Tamino Schemas. Because TSD files are plain text files, you can also open and edit them in any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), or GitHub Atom (cross-platform). Windows Tamino Schema Editor. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Linux Tamino Schema Editor. Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "Windows Tamino Schema Editor. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Linux Tamino Schema Editor. Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".MAW",
    "Access Data Access Page",
    "3.0",
    "Document created by the Microsoft Access desktop relational database software; may include hyperlinks, text fields, and submit buttons; used as a front-end for accessing the data in an Access database. NOTE: MAW files are often blocked by default in email server and client programs. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".IPJ",
    "ProFicient SPC Manufacturing Intelligence Project File",
    "3.0",
    "An IPJ file is a project file created by Autodesk Inventor, a CAD application used to create 3D prototypes of mechanical products. It contains XML data, including a reference to the location at which an Inventor projects files are stored. IPJ files help Inventor users organize, keep track of, and create links between other Inventor files. IPJ file open in Microsoft Visual Studio Code In Autodesk Inventor, engineers and product designers create 3D models that represent mechanical parts and assemblies. Assemblies can be comprised of many part files and other assembly files. Additionally, users can create drawings and presentations that show details of their assemblies. These drawings and presentations contain references to the assembly and part files used to create them. To ensure that links between dependent files remain valid, users save related files as part of a single Inventor project, which is loaded using an IPJ file. The IPJ file contains a record of the folder(s) in which a projects constituent files are stored, as well as other project-related settings. The IPJ file is often stored in a folder one level up from the folder containing a projects content. How do I switch between Inventor projects? If you need to switch between Inventor projects, close all your currently open Inventor files and then select File → Open from the programs menu bar. When the Open window appears, select the Projects.. button located next to the Project File field. This will open the Projects window, allowing you to browse to and select a different IPJ file. You can open an IPJ file in Autodesk Inventor (Windows). To do so, first close any currently open Inventor files. Then, from Inventors toolbar, select Get Started → Projects. The Projects window will appear, allowing you to browse to and open your IPJ file. If you want to view the XML data your IPJ file contains, you can also open it in any text or source code editor. However, you should never edit an IPJ files text, as doing so might cause your project to load incorrectly in Inventor. Windows Autodesk Inventor 2022. Okino Computer Graphics PolyTrans. An IPJ file is a project file created by InfinityQS ProFicient SPC Manufacturing Intelligence, a statistical process control program. It contains quality control data and Control Charts used to analyze that data. IPJ files can be opened only in ProFicient SPC Manufacturing Intelligence, and not other ProFicient suite applications. InfinityQS ProFicient is a suite of programs that allows manufacturers to analyze and improve upon their quality control and production. One of the programs ProFicient includes is SPC Manufacturing Intelligence (SPC MI). SPC MI allows quality control teams to gather and analyze production data, to ensure production is proceeding within acceptable quality control specifications. In SPC MI, data is organized into projects, which are often used to measure data for a specific process or product. SPC MI projects are saved as IPJ files. These files include all the data that has been automatically or manually entered into the projects database, as well as any Control Charts that have been created to analyze the data. IPJ files may include data for one or more manufacturing locations, which is often organized within separate, location-specific sheets. NOTE: SPC MI automatically creates backup project files each time a project is saved. These files use the.BAK extension. You can open an IPJ file in InfinityQS ProFicient SPC Manufacturing Intelligence (Windows). To do so, open ProFicient, select Project → Open, and then navigate to and open your IPJ file. When ProFicient prompts you to enter your user credentials, enter them and click OK. Windows InfinityQS ProFicient.",
    "Windows Autodesk Inventor 2022. Okino Computer Graphics PolyTrans. Windows InfinityQS ProFicient.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".SPQ",
    "SPSS Database Query File",
    "3.0",
    "File created by SPSS data mining and statistical analysis software; saves a query to a database; specifies the ODBC database type (e.g., MS Access, dBASE, Excel file), the data fields to extract, and transformations that write the data to the desired format. SPQ files allow SPSS users to save queries so that they can be run repeatedly. This is useful for updating the dataset when the data in the source database changes. SPSS query files can be run using the File → Open Database → Run Query.. dialog. They can be created in the Database Wizard, which you can access from the File → Open Database → New Query.. application menu option. Windows IBM SPSS. Mac IBM SPSS. Linux IBM SPSS.",
    "Windows IBM SPSS. Mac IBM SPSS. Linux IBM SPSS.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".FDB",
    "Legacy Family Tree Database",
    "3.0",
    "Primary database of images used by Extensis Portfolio, an image organization program; contains a thumbnail image and metadata for each file stored in the catalog. Windows Extensis Portfolio. Mac Extensis Portfolio. Database that stores financial information for a Microsoft Dynamics NAV project; used for business administration and management; can be accessed by other programs that support ODBC connections. Microsoft Dynamics NAV was previously called Microsoft Navision. Windows Microsoft Dynamics NAV or Navision. Database of clip art images stored in an Art Explosion collection; contains metadata and a thumbnail image for each picture referenced in the catalog. Art Explosion is popular clip art collection distributed by Nova Development. Windows Nova Development Art Explosion Extensis Portfolio Browser Mac Nova Development Art Explosion Extensis Portfolio Browser. An FDB is a database file created by Firebird, an open source SQL relational database management system (RDBMS). It contains an entire database, which includes one or more tables of rows and columns of data. FDB files are typically used to store data for web applications and software. You will most likely only encounter FDB files if you are the database architect or developer and utilize Firebird as your database solution. You can create and open FDB database files with the Database Explorer tool in Firebird. NOTE: Firebird is an open source fork from the Borland edition of the Interbase database. It was initially released in 2000 and has been continually developed. Windows Firebird. Mac Firebird. Linux FirebirdFree. An FDB file is a family tree database created by Legacy Family Tree. It contains information about a persons family tree, including a list of that persons ancestors and descendants. It may also contain birthdates, death dates, buried dates, and other information about each person included in the tree. FDB file open in Legacy Family Tree Legacy Family Tree is an ancestry application that allows users to import or create a family tree. The user can then add additional information about each family member, including stories and other identifying characteristics. Each family tree is saved as an FDB database file. Users can view the information an FDB file contains in many different formats, including family-, pedigree-, descendant-, chronology-, and index-based formats. Users can also transfer their family tree to Legacy Charting, for use as an.LWCX chart file. You can open an FDB file with Legacy Family Tree (Windows): Select File → Open File. Navigate to and open your FDB file. Windows Legacy Family Tree.",
    "Windows Extensis Portfolio. Mac Extensis Portfolio. Windows Microsoft Dynamics NAV or Navision. Windows Nova Development Art Explosion Extensis Portfolio Browser. Mac Nova Development Art Explosion Extensis Portfolio Browser. Windows Firebird. Mac Firebird. Linux Firebird. Windows Legacy Family Tree.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".TRASH_DATABASE",
    "Files by Google Trash Database",
    "3.0",
    "A TRASH_DATABASE file contains a list of files that a Files by Google user has moved to the apps Trash folder. It is a SQLite 3 database (.SQLITE) that is also located in the Trash folder. Files by Google uses the TRASH_DATABASE file to restore trashed files to their previous locations. TRASH_DATABASE file open in Apple TextEdit In 2020, Google added the ability to trash files to Files by Google, the default Android file manager. When you trash a file, it is placed in Files by Googles Trash folder and given a new.trashed filename. For up to 30 days, you can restore a trashed file to its previous location. To help Files by Google replace restored files, the app maintains a TRASH_DATABASE file. This file contains a list of the locations at which trashed files previously resided and the files original names. When you restore a trashed file, Files by Google uses the data its TRASH_DATABASE file contains to place the file where it belongs. TRASH_DATABASE files are not meant to be opened. Editing a TRASH_DATABASE file may affect your ability to restore trashed items in Files by Google. Android Files by GoogleFree.",
    "Android Files by Google.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DQY",
    "Microsoft Excel Query",
    "3.0",
    "A DQY file is a database query used by Microsoft Excel, a popular spreadsheet application. It stores a query defined with Microsoft Query or the Query Wizard included with Excel that accesses an external database to retrieve data and import it into an Excel spreadsheet. DQY files are saved in the ODBC standard for compatibility with other databases. Most Excel users will not create or open DQY files. However, advanced users looking to import data from a database may create and open DQY files since they are useful for saving queries to be used again. To create a DQY file with Query Wizard or Microsoft Query in Excel 365, follow these steps: Select Get Data in the Data tab Choose From Other Sources → From Microsoft Query Verify that the Use the Query Wizard to create/edit queries checkbox is checked in the Choose Data Source dialog Select the data source, click OK, choose the database you want to query, and define the query DQY files created with the Query Wizard or Microsoft Query in Excel 365 are saved in the following location, by default: C:/​Users/​[username]/​AppData/​Roaming/​Microsoft/​Queries NOTE: DQY files are primarily used by Excel 2007 to 365 users. You can open DQY files with Microsoft Excel in Windows and macOS. There are several ways to open a DQY file. To open the query directly from Excel 365: Select Get Data in the Data tab Choose From Other Sources → From Microsoft Query Click the Queries tab in the Choose Data Source dialog, select the query, then click Open To open the query directly from Microsoft Query (included with Excel), select File → Open.. NOTE: You can also select File → Open and choose the DQY file in Excel 365 or double-click a DQY file if it is associated with Excel. These options will run the query and insert the data into a new worksheet. Windows Microsoft Excel 365. Mac Microsoft Excel 365.",
    "Windows Microsoft Excel 365. Mac Microsoft Excel 365.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ANB",
    "Analysts Notebook Chart",
    "3.0",
    "An ANB file is an analytical chart created by IBM i2 Analysts Notebook, a data analysis program. It contains a diagram that explains how different pieces of information are connected to each other. ANB files are comprised of entities, which represent pieces of information, links, which show that entities are connected, and properties, which describe an entity or link in more detail. Data analysts and investigators use IBM i2 Analysts Notebook to review data and help them find previously unnoticed patterns and connections. For example, an analyst at a government agency may use Analysts Notebook to investigate a suspected case of tax fraud, in hopes of bringing a criminal to justice. In Analysts Notebook, users conduct analyses by importing or entering relevant information and then either manually or programmatically finding connections between those pieces of information. Analysts Notebook displays these networks of information to users as diagrams, referred to as analytical charts. When a user wants to save an in-progress chart, they can do so by saving the chart as an ANB file. The ANB file contains all data displayed on the chart, including entered information, links, properties, labels, and legends. You can open an ANB file in IBM i2 Analysts Notebook (Windows) or IMB i2 Chart Reader (Windows). Chart Reader is a free application that allows users to view the chart an ANB file contains. However, users must create an IBM account before they can download Chart Reader. Windows IBM i2 Analysts Notebook. IBM i2 Chart ReaderFree.",
    "Windows IBM i2 Analysts Notebook. IBM i2 Chart Reader.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".BACPAC",
    "Compressed Microsoft SQL Database",
    "3.0",
    "A BACPAC file is a Zip-compressed archive that contains a Microsoft SQL databases schema and data. Users export BACPAC files from and import BACPAC files into Microsoft SQL database programs, such as Microsoft Azure SQL Database and Microsoft SQL Server. BACPAC files are used to transfer databases between servers. Database managers can use a variety of Microsoft SQL database management tools to export databases as BACPAC files. For example: Azure users can export a database as a BACPAC file from the Azure portal SQL Database users can export a database as a BACPAC file using the SqlPackage command-line utility SQL Server Management Studio users can export a database as a BACPAC file using a wizard included in that application While BACPAC files are similar to.DACPAC files, the files are used for different purposes. BACPAC files are used primarily to back up or move databases from one server to another. DACPAC files are focused on capturing and deploying schema. Sometimes, DACPAC files are applied to existing databases. You can import the database a BACPAC file contains into Microsoft Azure SQL Database or Microsoft SQL Server. To do so, you must use either: The Import Data-tier Application menu item (found by opening Object Explorer, right-clicking on Databases, and then selecting Import Data-tier Application) available in Microsoft SQL Server (Windows) The Import database option available in the SQL server section of the Microsoft Azure portal The SqlPackage command-line utility. Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019. Web Microsoft Azure SQL Database.",
    "Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019. Web Microsoft Azure SQL Database.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".CAF",
    "Cathy Catalog File",
    "3.0",
    "A CAF file is an audio file saved in the Core Audio Format (CAF), a digital audio format based on Apples Core Audio technology. It stores audio data, text annotations, markers, channel layouts, and other information. CAF files are similar to.AIFF and.WAVE files, but do not have a 4GB size limit and can store any number of audio channels. CAF file open in VideoLAN VLC media player 3 The CAF file structure includes a file header that stores information about the file type and CAF version and is followed by multiple data chunks. Two chunks always present in CAF files are the 1) Audio Data chunk, which contains the audio data, and the 2) Audio Description chunk, which contains information that specifies the audio data format. Other types of chunks include the following: Channel Layout - Required for CAF files with more than one audio channel; describes the role of each channel in the file. Information - Stores text about the audio data, which includes the title and artist. Edit Comments - Contains time-stamped comments added when the CAF data is edited. Instrument - Stores descriptive information about audio data needed when the audio is used by a sampler or played as an instrument. NOTE: For more information about CAF, view Apples documentation. You can open CAF files with various audio players, including QuickTime Player 7 and later (included with macOS), VideoLAN VLC media player (multiplatform), Audacity (multiplatform), and NCH WavePad (multiplatform). The CAF audio format is supported by Mac OS X (10.4 and later) applications that incorporate the Core Audio API. The format is also supported by iOS, beginning with version 5.0. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. VideoLAN VLC media playerer GoldWave. Audacity. NCH WavePad. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Apple GarageBand Included with OS. Apple Logic Pro. Apple Final Cut Express —  (Discontinued). Apple Final Cut Pro. VideoLAN VLC media player. ShedWorx Smart Converter. Audacity. NCH WavePad. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. AudacityFree. File created by the CryENGINE SDK, an application suite used for making PC and console games; contains character animation data that was compiled from a.CHR character file using a.CBA compiler specification file. CAF files are used as intermediate compilation files before building the database animation (.DBA) file, which is suitable for use in the final game deliverable. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK. Gradebook file created by Class Action Gradebook, a program used for organizing classroom information; may contain student information, seating arrangements, homework assignments, awarded grades, and other class data. CAF files are used for managing gradebook data and for printing reports. Teachers can generate reports such as classroom grade summaries, individual student reports, parent letters, and class and assignment graphs. Each report can be customized. NOTE: CAF files are created by the Secondary and College editions of Class Action Gradebook. Windows CalEd Class Action Gradebook —  (Discontinued). A CAF file is a catalog created by the Cathy media cataloging tool. It contains an indexed catalog of media files that users can search through within Cathy. CAF files can be shared with other Cathy users to allow them to browse your media collection. Cathy is a free media cataloging program that music and movie enthusiasts can use to catalog the CDs, DVDs,.MP3s,.MP4s, and other media that they own. When a user saves a catalog within Cathy, it is saved as a CAF file. After creating a CAF catalog, users can search the catalog by filename, the date a file was created, or file size. Sometimes, Cathy users share their CAF catalogs with others, allowing those users to peruse their media collection. Note that sharing your CAF catalog with someone wont allow that person to actually play your media. However, it will allow you to compare the pieces of media you own (and maybe, inspire you to swap some files). You can open a CAF file in Cathy. To do so, place your CAF file in the same directory as your Cathy.exe file. Then, open Cathy. Your CAF catalog will appear in Cathy. Windows CathyFree. Three-dimensional animation file used by Cal3D, a free toolkit used for character modeling and animation; contains motion settings for the models skeleton; specifies rotations and movements for the models bones over time. CAF files are used to give characters realistic human motions. They can specify animations for walking, running, or various other movements. NOTE: Cal3D animation files can also be expressed in an XML format using.XAF files. Windows Cal3dViewer. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3DFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. VideoLAN VLC media playerer GoldWave. Audacity. NCH WavePad. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Apple GarageBand Included with OS. Apple Logic Pro. Apple Final Cut Express —  (Discontinued). Apple Final Cut Pro. VideoLAN VLC media player. ShedWorx Smart Converter. Audacity. NCH WavePad. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. Audacity. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK. Windows CalEd Class Action Gradebook —  (Discontinued). Windows Cathy. Windows Cal3dViewer. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3D.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".MRG",
    "MySQL Merge File",
    "3.0",
    "Merge template created by Now Contact, an application that organizes contact information and day-to-day activities; contains a print layout template for your letter document; pre-loaded options include Fancy Letter, Flower Letter, Swoosh Letter, and Ship Letter.. To create the MRG file, select Define → Print Templates → Faxes.., select the + button in the top-right, name the template, and click OK. You will then be able to edit the template layout and its dimensions. Click OK when youre finished. When creating a new.NWP letter document, you can select a MRG template to work off of by choosing a template from the Use Template drop down menu. To select the template you want to print from, select File → Print Templates.., choose your template from the Template Type drop down menu, and click OK. Windows Now Contact. Mac Now ContactFree. Database file used by MySQL, a free, open source relational database program; contains the names of tables that are used as a single table in a MySQL merge table scheme; created by the MySQL MERGE storage engine. MRG files are saved with a.FRM file that contains the structure for the tables in the merge table. Windows MySQL. Mac MySQL. Linux MySQL.",
    "Windows Now Contact. Mac Now Contact. Windows MySQL. Mac MySQL. Linux MySQL.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".KEXI",
    "Kexi Database",
    "3.0",
    "Database file created by Kexi, a database program that can be used as an alternative to Microsoft Access on Linux systems; supports database schemas, data, queries, forms, and other database information. Linux KexiFree.",
    "Linux Kexi.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".FTB",
    "Family Tree Builder Genealogy Database File",
    "3.0",
    "An FTB file is a database file used by MyHeritage Family Tree Builder, a free genealogy application. It contains genealogy data, which may include details about people in a family tree, relationships between relatives, photos, charts, and maps. FTB file open in MyHeritage Family Tree Builder 8 FTB files were introduced with the release of version 8 of MyHeritage Family Tree Builder. The files are saved in an SQLite database format, which is more efficient than the Zip-compressed.ZED and.UZED database files it replaced. ZED files are primarily used by versions 1 - 6 of Family Tree Builder and UZED files are primarily used by version 7 of the software. To create an FTB file with Family Tree Builder, select File → New Project.. The software automatically saves modifications to the project database. Family Tree Builder saves FTB files by default in the following directory: C:/​Users/​[username]/​Documents/​MyHeritage/​[Project name]/​Database/​. You can only open FTB files with version 8 or later of Family Tree Builder. To open an FTB file with the software, select File → Open Project... Windows MyHeritage Family Tree Builder. Mac MyHeritage Family Tree BuilderFree.",
    "Windows MyHeritage Family Tree Builder. Mac MyHeritage Family Tree Builder.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".NRMLIB",
    "Neat Cabinet File",
    "3.0",
    "Cabinet file created by Neat 5, a digital filing system; contains a library of your scanned documents; used only by the Mac version of Neat and not the Windows version of the software. To create a NRMLIB file, select File → New → Cabinet.., name the file , choose the save location, and click Save You can create a backup of your NRMLIB file by simply copying your file from its save location (most likely in your Documents folder) and paste it to the location youd like to keep the backup. Neat Library.nrmlib - The default name given to your cabinet file when you first open Neat. Mac Neat.",
    "Mac Neat.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".XMLFF",
    "XML Flat File",
    "3.0",
    "Database file format developed by Control Split; contains XML schema merged with Python arrays in plain text format. The XMLFF format is similar to XML but also supports data that is not encased within a parent child schema. The purpose of the format is to work with database methods in.PY files and to provide users with an open source flat file database solution. Windows Any text editor Mac Any text editor Linux Any text editor.",
    "Windows Any text editor. Mac Any text editor. Linux Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DAD",
    "RemObjects Data Abstract Driver File",
    "3.0",
    "Driver file used by RemObjects middle-tier applications; contains a driver, which communicates with a database server to supply data for the middle-tier application; can be swapped out dynamically during runtime to switch data providers. Windows RemObjects SDK. RemObjects Data Abstract. A DAD file is a video file created by Sysvideo Technology IMS200, a professional security system program. It contains video recorded by a security camera and downloaded using the IMS200 security system software. IMS200 is a free program that allows users to manage a professional security system. The program can be used by multiple users to control multiple cameras and manage recorded security footage. You can download footage by selecting a video record from a specific device, right clicking the file and selecting Start Download or simply double-clicking the record. The footage is then saved in a DAD file. Windows Sysvideo Technology IMS200.",
    "Windows RemObjects SDK. RemObjects Data Abstract. Windows Sysvideo Technology IMS200.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".IDB",
    "IDA Database File",
    "2.9",
    "Intermediate file created by a Visual Studio program, such as Visual C++, during the debugging process; saves the compilers state and is used for minimal program rebuilds and incremental compilations. Windows Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. File created by IDA (The Interactive Disassembler), a program that disassembles executable files (.EXE) into low-level assembly language code; stores the disassembled data in a compressed format; used in the process of exploring executables, often for revealing potential security threats or exploitation routes. When an IDB file is opened in IDA, the data is decompressed into a collection of files. After the database is closed, the files are then compressed back into the IDB file. This enables faster performance while the database is open and lower disk usage when closed. Windows Hex-Rays IDA.",
    "Windows Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Windows Hex-Rays IDA.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".NV",
    "NewViews Database File",
    "2.9",
    "Database file created by NewViews for DOS (also referred to as NV1), a DOS program used for business accounting; can include payroll, tax, expense, income, and other accounting information; used for storing and tracking company finances. NV files can be converted to the newer.NV2 format using a NewViews for DOS component called NVEXPORT, a procedure library made available by Q.W. Page. After conversion, the created file can be opened by NewViews 2 the first time NewViews 2 is opened. NOTE: NewViews for DOS was originally released in 1986. That year it won PC Magazines award for Technical Excellence. The software is still used by some organizations that have not transitioned to NewViews 2 (NV2) for Windows. Windows Q.W. Page NewViews for DOS. Game data file created by MAME arcade emulation programs; often contains game settings and high score saved information; used for emulating the Non-Volatile RAM (NVRAM) hardware on the arcade. NV files are only used by some MAME games, while others use different save data files, such as.HI files. Windows MAME. ExtraMAME. Mac MacMAME MAME OS XFree.",
    "Windows Q.W. Page NewViews for DOS. Windows MAME. ExtraMAME. Mac MacMAME MAME OS X.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ACCDW",
    "Microsoft Access Database Link File",
    "2.8",
    "Link file used by Microsoft Access, a relational database program for desktop computers; contains link information for downloading an Access database file (.ACCDB file) from a Microsoft SharePoint server; enables users to share database files that are hosted remotely. After an ACCDW file is opened, the target ACCDB file is automatically downloaded to a local copy on the users computer. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ECX",
    "ECCO Corrupted Database File",
    "2.8",
    "Database file created with ECCO, a personal information management (PIM) program; may contain corrupted data that cannot be read by ECCO. If ECCO notices a file has been corrupted, it may save it with a .ecx extension rather than the usual.ECO file extension. May be generated during the Create Synchronized Copy process. Windows NetManage ECCO or ECCO Pro.",
    "Windows NetManage ECCO or ECCO Pro.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".SBF",
    "Superbase Database",
    "2.8",
    "System file used by Google Android devices, such as Motorola DROID 2 and DROID X mobile phones; contains all phone data as it was originally configured from the factory; enables the phone to be set to the original factory settings. NOTE: The program RSD Lite can be used to flash an SBF file to a Motorola DROID 2 or DROID X phone. Generally, users should not manually restore SBF files, since improper use of the files can cause the phone to malfunction. Windows Motorola RSD Lite Android Google Android Included with OS. An SBF file is a database created by Superbase, a program used to create and manage databases. It contains data stored in records, which can consist of 1 to 999 fields. SBF files are saved in a binary format. In 1983, Precision Software released the original version of Superbase for the Commodore 64 and 128. Later, the company also made Superbase available for the Amiga, Atari ST, and Windows. Various other publishers have released subsequent versions of Superbase, including 2003s Superbase Classic and 2016s Superbase NG. Databases created by Superbase are saved as SBF files. Users and applications created in Superbase can perform various functions on these databases, such as searching them for information, updating them, and creating reports using their data. You can open an SBF file with various versions of Superbase (Windows), such as Superbase Classic and Superbase NG. Note that if your SBF file was created by an old version of Superbase, you may have to convert the file to Superbases current database format before you can open it. Windows Superbase Software Superbase NG. Superbase Software Superbase Classic. Data file format used by SmartBroker stock tracking software; may contain stock lists, trend data, news headlines, tracking reports, or other data. Windows SmartBroker Pro. An SBF file is a GPS data file created by Septentrio GNSS receivers, which are electronic devices that receive and process signals from global navigation satellite system (GNSS) satellites. It contains a data log about the GPS position, time, and velocity of a device fitted with a GNSS receiver. SBF files are saved in binary format to reduce file size. Septentrio GNSS receivers are used in a large variety of industries, which include geographic information systems, scientific and unmanned aerial vehicles, marine, construction, agriculture, and survey and mapping. SBF files are used to store the data logs for devices used in these industries. SBF files may be opened by a variety of tools from the Septentrio RxTools suite, which include SBF Analyzer and SBF Converter. You can convert SBF files using the SBF Converter to several formats, such as ASCII, KML, GPX, and RINEX. The tools can be found in the rools/​binary/​win32 subdirectory in the installation path. Windows Septentrio RxTools. Septentrio PP-SDK.",
    "Windows Motorola RSD Lite. Android Google Android Included with OS. Windows Superbase Software Superbase NG. Superbase Software Superbase Classic. Windows SmartBroker Pro. Windows Septentrio RxTools. Septentrio PP-SDK.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".FMP",
    "FileMaker Pro Database",
    "2.8",
    "An FMP file is a dropdown menu created with 123 Flash Menu, a Flash-based web menu creation program. It includes the menus style, fonts, colors, dimensions, sounds, and animations. FMP files can be exported as standard Flash (.SWF) files that can be inserted into webpages. Windows Dreamingsoft 123 Flash Menu. Font settings file used by AutoCAD, a CAD program used for drawing and documenting 2D and 3D designs; stores a mapping between a list of fonts and their substitutes; commonly includes references to.PFB,.SHX, and.TTF files; opened by AutoCAD when a default font cannot be found in order to locate the replacement font to be used. FMP files are saved in plain text and can be edited with a text editor. They store substitutions separated by line breaks in the following format: original_font;replacement_font_file The default AutoCAD font map file has the name acad.fmp for AutoCAD and acadlt.fmp for AutoCAD LT. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. An FMP file is a database created by Claris FileMaker Pro, a data management program for Windows and macOS. It contains business data organized into tables and records. Users commonly refer to databases created by specific versions of FileMaker Pro as FMP files, even though those files actually use different, version-specific file extensions. You can open an FMP file with FileMaker Pro (Windows, Mac). Note, however, that if your file uses the.fmp extension, youll likely have to change the extension to one of the correct, version-specific extensions listed above. Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced. Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced.",
    "Windows Dreamingsoft 123 Flash Menu. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced. Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced.",
    "For example, while asking for help with FileMaker Pro 5, a user may refer to a database they created as an FMP file. This is because FMP is a common abbreviation for FileMaker Pro. However, FileMaker Pro 5 actually saves databases as.FP5 files. Thus, the users file is likely an FP5 file. Other versions of FileMaker Pro save databases with the following file extensions:.FM - FileMaker Pro 2.FP3 - FileMaker Pro 3.FP4 - FileMaker Pro 4.FP5 - FileMaker Pro 5 and 6.FP7 - FileMaker Pro 7 - 11.FMP12 - FileMaker Pro 12 and above."],
    ["database_files",
    ".MFD",
    "Music Finder Database",
    "2.8",
    "An MFD file is a database used by Yamaha keyboards, such as the PSR, PSR-S, Tyros, and CVP models. It contains a collection of songs that include the song number, title, genre, style, tempo, and keywords. MFD file open in MusicFinderView Many Yamaha keyboard models come with preset MFD database files. Music Finder is a feature that allows you to search the MFD files. When you search through your keyboard for songs with different styles and tempos, Music Finder searches the songs stored in the MFD databases. If you come across an MFD file on your computer you can open it in Windows with the MusicFinderView program. The program allows you to modify, replace, or delete songs. MusicFinderView also enables you to rearrange, sort, and print the list of songs stored in the file. Windows MusicFinderViewFree.",
    "Windows MusicFinderView.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".JET",
    "JET Database File",
    "2.7",
    "A JET file is a settings file used by The Jackbox Party Pack series of video games. It contains JSON- or XML-formatted text that defines settings for a specific Party Pack party game. For example, in The Jackbox Party Pack 2, the game Earwax uses a JET file named EarwaxAudio.jet to retrieve and play audio files. JET file open in Microsoft Visual Studio Code The Jackbox Party Pack is a series of video games that each include a set of party games. For example, The Jackbox Party Pack 2 includes five party games: Fibbage 2, Earwax, Bidiots, Quiplash XL, and Bomb Corp. Each Jackbox party game uses unique game data stored in a game-specific sub-directory. For example, Earwax stores its game data in the following directory: ~/​Jackbox Games/​The Jackbox Party Pack 2/​games/​Earwax Each party games data includes one or more JET settings files. These files determine, for example, what text and what media files are shown at certain points in the game. All JET files are plain text files, which modders can edit to modify what text, images, and sounds appear in a game. Because JET files are plain text files, you can open and edit them in any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad or Apple TextEdit. Be careful when editing a JET file, as editing the file incorrectly could cause the associated Jackbox party game to function incorrectly. Windows The Jackbox Party Pack. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor Mac The Jackbox Party Pack. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Any text editor Linux The Jackbox Party Pack. Vim. Any text editor. Database file created by the Microsoft Joint Engine Technology (JET) Engine; contains a database structure, which includes tables and fields, and table row database entries in the JET format. The Microsoft JET Engine is a SQL database engine that was distributed with several different Microsoft applications, including Microsoft Access. However, Microsoft no longer supports JET and has moved to SQL Server. You can still open JET database files by renaming the jet file extension to mdb, which enables the file to be opened by Microsoft Access. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "Windows The Jackbox Party Pack. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor. Mac The Jackbox Party Pack. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Any text editor. Linux The Jackbox Party Pack. Vim. Any text editor. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".TMD",
    "MySQL Temporary Database File",
    "2.7",
    "Document created by TextMaker, a word processing application that is part of SoftMaker Office; supports text, images, drawn objects, and page formatting properties; used to store authored documents. TMD files were replaced by.TMDX files. Android SoftMaker Office HD: TextMaker BASIC. Windows SoftMaker Office. Linux SoftMaker Office. A TMD file contains title metadata used to verify the integrity and run Nintendo 3DS, Wii, and WiiU games. It stores metadata about the file that contains the actual game data, such as an APP, 3DS, or CIA file, and is referenced to decrypt and verify the contents of the game data file to launch the game. TMD files are typically distributed by Nintendo Update Servers (NUS). TMD files may store varying metadata depending on the console the game is created to run on. For example, a TMD file for a WiiU game contains the required WiiUOS version, whereas a TMD file for a 3DS game will not include that information. Most 3DS, Wii, and WiiU gamers will not encounter a TMD file since it is referenced by the Nintendo console in the background when a game is launched. However, gamers who want to emulate a game on their computers will most likely see the TMD file (along with a TIK and CERT file) accompanying the main game data file. Windows Citra. Mac Citra. Linux CitraFree. 3D model used by some games for the PlayStation console systems; saves the geometry (vertices and shapes) for the three-dimensional image; used for game characters, scenery, monsters, and other game objects. An example PlayStation game that uses TMD files is Jurassic Park: Operation Genesis. Some TMD files can be viewed with MilkShape 3D, but without the coloring. Windows chUmbaLum sOft MilkShape 3DFree. Intermediate database file created by MySQL, an open source relational database program; contains information that helps MySQL complete database recoveries or conversion processes; created in the database directory where the.MYI,.MYD, and.FRM files are located. TMD files can be created when the myisampack MySQL command is run. If the process is terminated before completion, the temporary TMD files might not be deleted. TMD files may also be created by other MySQL database operations. Windows MySQL. Mac MySQL. Linux MySQL. A TMD file is a 3D world created by World Machine, a program used to procedurally generate terrain for video games. It contains a series of devices that World Machine uses to generate terrain. TMD files can be opened only in World Machine. TMD file open in World Machine World Machine allows developers to procedurally generate realistic-looking 3D terrain for use in video games and other applications. To generate terrain, a developer links a series of World Machine devices together. These devices control how World Machine shapes the developers terrain. Devices can be used to create new terrain, edit existing terrain, and export terrain to different file formats. If a developer wants to save an in-progress or finished World Machine project, they can select File → Save World from the programs menu bar. This saves the developers current world as a TMD file. When a developer selects Build World from World Machines menu, World Machine uses the device tree the developer has assembled to generate terrain. World Machine will also export the terrain in additional file formats, if the device tree includes output devices configured to export terrain. NOTE: To view the devices a TMD file contains, view the file in World Machines Device Workview. To view the terrain those devices generate, view the file in the Layout or 3D View. You can open a TMD file in World Machine (Windows). To do so, select File → Open World.. from World Machines menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your TMD file. Windows World Machine Software World Machine.",
    "Android SoftMaker Office HD: TextMaker BASIC. Windows SoftMaker Office. Linux SoftMaker Office. Windows Citra. Mac Citra. Linux Citra. Windows chUmbaLum sOft MilkShape 3D. Windows MySQL. Mac MySQL. Linux MySQL. Windows World Machine Software World Machine.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".RSD",
    "RealSQLDatabase File",
    "2.7",
    "An RSD file is a data file created for Rosetta Stone, an interactive language teaching program. It contains language data referenced by Rosetta Stone and is not meant to be manually opened. RSD files are located in the data and speech folders within the Rosetta Stone.ISO file on the Language Disc. Windows Rosetta Stone Language Learning. Mac Rosetta Stone Language Learning. An RSD file is a database file format used by REALbasic, a software development application that uses the BASIC programming language. RSD files store data in a structured format that can be accessed via SQL commands. RealSQLDatabase files may be loaded within a REALbasic program using a command such as: myDB.databaseFile = GetFolderItem(mydb.rsd). In 2013, REALbasic became Xojo. The legacy RSD file extension may still be used by some Xojo developers on SQLite files instead of.SQLITE. Windows REAL Software REALbasic 5 or later Xojo. Mac REAL Software REALbasic 5 or later Xojo. Linux REAL Software REALbasic 5 or later Xojo. An RSD file is an audio file used by a Radical Entertainment video game, such as The Simpsons: Hit & Run and The Incredible Hulk: Ultimate Destruction. It contains music, dialogue, sound effects, or other audio played in the game. Radical Entertainment was a Canadian video game development company that developed several popular games, including some games in the Crash Bandicoot series. Many of Radical Entertainments games included audio files saved in the companys proprietary RSD file format. NOTE: The game MadWorld, published by RedSpark, also uses RSD audio files. However, RedSparks RSD files are saved in a different format than Radical Entertainments RSD files. Gamers who want to play an RSD file can do so using the vgmstream plug-in, which is available for Foobar2000 (Windows) and Nullsoft Winamp (Windows). Gamers can also convert RSD files to other audio formats using Lucas RSD Converter (Windows). Windows Foobar2000 with vgmstream plug-in. Nullsoft Winamp with vgmstream plug-in. Lucas RSD ConverterFree. An RSD file is a game data file used by Donkey Kong Country Tropical Freeze. It contains data used to load a level. For example, RSD files contain data used to load a levels geometry, layers, and objects. In 2014, Retro Studios and Monster Games released Donkey Kong Country Tropical Freeze, a platforming game for the Wii U. The game includes many types of game data files, including RSD files. These files are saved in proprietary formats, and they are not meant to be opened or edited by players. RSD files are not meant to be opened. No programs available.",
    " Windows Rosetta Stone Language Learning. Mac Rosetta Stone Language Learning. Windows REAL Software REALbasic 5 or later Xojo. Mac REAL Software REALbasic 5 or later Xojo. Linux REAL Software REALbasic 5 or later Xojo. Windows Foobar2000 with vgmstream plug-in. Nullsoft Winamp with vgmstream plug-in. Lucas RSD Converter. No programs available.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DSK",
    "Simple IDs Database",
    "2.7",
    "Generic disk image format created by disk imaging programs; may be from an older program that images 3.5 diskettes, or from a newer program that creates larger disk images; often compressed to save disk space; can be mounted to appear as a disk on the desktop for Mac or within My Computer for Windows. NOTE: Since the .dsk extension is used as a generic marker for multiple types of disk images, a DSK file created in one program may not be compatible with another program. Windows SoftAmbulance Partition Doctor. PowerISO. R-Tools Technology R-Studio. Smart Projects IsoBuster. Mac Apple Disk Utility Included with OS. Project file created by Borland Delphi or C++ development software; may store several files and resources referenced by the project. Windows Embarcadero Delphi. Database of ID cards created by Simple IDs, an identification card creator program. Windows DSKE Simple IDs.",
    "Windows SoftAmbulance Partition Doctor. PowerISO. R-Tools Technology R-Studio. Smart Projects IsoBuster. Mac Apple Disk Utility Included with OS. Windows Embarcadero Delphi. Windows DSKE Simple IDs.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".CKP",
    "SQL Server Checkpoint File",
    "2.7",
    "Database file created by SQL Server, a relational database application; created by SQL Server when performing a restore so that the restore operation can be restarted if a failure occurs; stores database log information that is written during the restore. Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019.",
    "Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".MDT",
    "GeoMedia Access Database Template",
    "2.7",
    "Data file used by Microsoft Access, a relational database management system (RDBMS) for desktop computers; stores data used for the software and may include data for software add-ins. Windows Microsoft Access 365. Database template file used by GeoMedia, a software package used for geospatial processing; saves the default structure of an Access database and can be used for initializing an Access database (.MDB) file with geospatial data. The default Access database template used by GeoMedia is saved in the file normal.mdt. Windows Intergraph GeoMedia —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows Microsoft Access 365. Windows Intergraph GeoMedia —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ADB",
    "Ability Database File",
    "2.7",
    "Programming file containing source code written in the Ada programming language; stores the body of an Ada program; typically saved along with a corresponding Spec file that has an.ADS extension. Windows File Viewer Plus. Any text editor Mac MacroMates TextMate. Any text editor Linux gcc gnat Any text editor. File used by Alpha Five, an IDE that allows users to develop Web applications; contains file names for all tables and libraries that are part of the database; stored as part of an overall database for Alpha Five developers. ADB files can be reused by other Alpha Five programs. NOTE: In 2013, Alpha Five became Alpha Anywhere. Windows Alpha Software Alpha Anywhere. Database file created by Ability Database, a desktop relational database program included with Ability Office; saves tables, forms, queries, reports, and macros for the database; used for storing address books, inventories, customer information, and other structured data. Ability database files are compatible with.MDB files created by Microsoft Access and can be exported to the MDB format. Windows Ability Office. Address book template created by Now Contact, an application that organizes contact information; contains a template print layout for your address book; pre-defined options include A4 Portfolio, DayRunner Classic, Organizer - 2 Column, and Portfolio - Basic.. To create the ADB file, select Define → Print Templates → Address Books.., select the + button in the top-right, name the template, and click OK. You can then edit the template layout and its dimensions. Click OK when youre finished. To select the template you want to print from, select File → Print Templates.., choose your template, and click OK. Windows Now Contact. Mac Now ContactFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus. Any text editor. Mac MacroMates TextMate. Any text editor. Linux gcc gnat Any text editor. Windows Alpha Software Alpha Anywhere. Windows Ability Office. Windows Now Contact. Mac Now Contact.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".MUD",
    "Textease Multi User Database",
    "2.7",
    "3D image created by Mudbox, a 3D digital sculpting and painting application; saves a 3D model with textures and lighting information; can include multiple sculpt and paint layers; can also incorporate models (.OBJ, and.FBX) created in other 3D software tools such as Maya. Mudbox scenes are created by digital art professionals and are used for still or animated digital art as well as for video game characters. NOTE: MUD files can be exported to a 16-bit Photoshop.PSD file for touch-ups. Windows Autodesk Mudbox 2022. Mac Autodesk Mudbox 2022. Linux Autodesk Mudbox 2022. Database created by Textease, an educational tool designed for Information Communications Technology (ICT) teaching purposes; created along with one or more.TE files; allows multiple students to add and modify data using a single database file. Textease Studio CT is no longer developed. Windows Lightbox Education Textease Studio CT.",
    "Windows Autodesk Mudbox 2022. Mac Autodesk Mudbox 2022. Linux Autodesk Mudbox 2022. Windows Lightbox Education Textease Studio CT.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".FP4",
    "FileMaker Pro 4 Database",
    "2.6",
    "An FP4 file is a database created by Claris FileMaker Pro 4. It contains one or more data tables, each of which includes labels and data records. Businesses use FP4 files to organize their inventories, finances, employees, and projects. FileMaker Pro is a data management program that allows businesses to input, organize, and review data. For example, a business might input its inventory list into a FileMaker Pro database and use the program to track and share its inventory. In 1997, Claris released the fourth version of FileMaker Pro, named FileMaker Pro 4. This version of the program saved users databases as FP4 files. Notably, Claris changed its name to FileMaker, Inc. before releasing FileMaker Pro 4.1. The company has since changed its name back to Claris. You can open an FP4 file with FileMaker Pro (Windows, Mac) versions 4 through 11. To open an FP4 file with a more recent version of FileMaker Pro, you must first convert the file to the current FileMaker Pro database format. For example, to open an FP4 file with FileMaker Pro 12, you must: Open the file with FileMaker Pro 11 to convert it to the.FP7 format. Open the converted FP7 file with FileMaker Pro 12 or a later version to convert it to the.FMP12 format. Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced. Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced.",
    "Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced. Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".NS2",
    "Lotus Notes 2 Database",
    "2.5",
    "Data file created by Lotus Notes 2.x; contains contact list, notebook, calendar, and other information; used to store contact information and to collaborate with other Lotus Notes users. Windows IBM Lotus Notes 2 or later Lotus Domino Mac IBM Lotus Notes 2 or later Lotus Domino.",
    "Windows IBM Lotus Notes 2 or later Lotus Domino. Mac IBM Lotus Notes 2 or later Lotus Domino.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ERX",
    "Entity Relationship Data Model File",
    "2.5",
    "An ERX file contains an Entity Relationship data model, which is a diagram that details the relationships between components of data in a database. It is used by various database software to design the structure of a database. Various programs may be used to create ERX files including erwin Data Modeler, Microsoft Dynamics, and Microsoft Visio. To create an ERX file with Microsoft Dynamics AX, click Tools → Reverse Engineer and select ERX ER Data Model. To create an ERX file with Visio, click File → Save As and choose the ERX format type. Windows Microsoft Visio 2021. Microsoft Dynamics AX. erwin Data Modeler.",
    "Windows Microsoft Visio 2021. Microsoft Dynamics AX. erwin Data Modeler.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".MAS",
    "Access Stored Procedures",
    "2.5",
    "Game file used by rFactor, a racing simulation game; stores the asset files for a racing track map and includes files for both the structure and the appearance of the track; can be modded to create custom tracks, but modding is only for advanced users. MAS files can be opened with the gMotor MAS File Utility (MAS.EXE), which is part of the rFactor mod development tool pack available from the rFactor website. Windows Image Space rFactor. gMotor MAS File Utility. Data file created by MEGA, a program used for testing evolutionary hypotheses; created in MEGAs Alignment Explorer tool and contains a binary representation of a genetic sequence alignment, which aligns genetic codes between two samples. MAS files are used for saving the computed sequence alignment result and performing additional analysis such as generating phylogenetic trees (.MTS files). Windows MEGA. Mac MEGAFree. Pre-written procedure or query used by an Access database. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "Windows Image Space rFactor. gMotor MAS File Utility. Windows MEGA. Mac MEGA. Windows Microsoft Access 365.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DADIAGRAMS",
    "RemObjects Data Abstract Data Diagrams File",
    "2.5",
    "Developer file created using the RemObjects SDK, a development application suite used for building middle-tier applications; contains a diagram of a database schemas that define how data is represented in the database. NOTE: Data Abstract schemas are stored using.DASCHEMA files. Windows RemObjects SDK. RemObjects Data Abstract.",
    "Windows RemObjects SDK. RemObjects Data Abstract.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".RBF",
    "Redatam Binary File",
    "2.5",
    "Archive of files created during a software installation process run by Windows Installer; contains files that can be restored if the installation does not successfully complete; if the installation is successful, the rollback file is automatically deleted. The RBF file is saved along with a corresponding.RBS script file and stored in an archive named Config.Msi.. Windows Microsoft Windows Installer Included with OS. An RBF file is an executable file used by the EV3 Intelligent Brick, which is a device used to control LEGO MINDSTORMS EV3 robots. It stores an EV3 Basic program, which is used to make a robot perform a function. RBF files are compiled by the built-in compiler in EV3 Explorer and executed directly on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. EV3 Basic programs are used to make LEGO MINDSTORMS EV3 robots perform a variety of tasks, whether it be moving a certain direction or picking up an object. These programs can be run in PC mode and brick mode. In PC mode, the programs runs in Microsoft Small Basic, while relaying information to the EV3 Intelligent Brick in order to operate the robot. However, in brick mode, the programs run on the EV3 Intelligent Brick, which is a portable device that features a Linux-based operating system and is used to interface with the robots. RBF files are used to run programs on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. RBF files are compiled from.SB files, which are files that store Small Basic program code, by EV3 Explorer, which is a Windows program used to view and organize files stored on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. EV3 Explorer can also be used to download RBF,.RSF, and.RGF files to the EV3 Intelligent Brick. Windows Executed on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. Mac Executed on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. Linux Executed on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. Backup image created by Insta Backup Gold, a Windows program used to backup and restore files; contains the backup data of a file, folder, volume, or email database. There are a number of settings that Insta Backup Gold provides for creating an RBF backup file. You can protect your backup with a password, select the compression level of your backup, and schedule backups to be created at a later time and at a custom frequency. Also, you can choose if you want a full, incremental, or a differential backup. NOTE: Stellar Insta Backup Gold has been discontinued. Windows Stellar Insta Backup Gold. File created by Retadam (Retrieval of Data for Small Areas by Microcomputer), a mapping software used for analyzing local and regional census and survey data; saves data as structured records in a compressed binary format; used for analyzing geographical areas from the size of a few city blocks to a whole country. RBF files may store census data such as gender, age, and household information. The data is stored in the form of entities (a logical hierarchy of objects) and variables (information on entities), which are further defined by the Retadam documentation. NOTE: The Retadam software is supported by the Economic Commission for Latin America and the Caribbean (CELADE). Windows CELADE REDATAMFree. Backup set containing data backed up with Retrospect backup software; contains actual files and folders backed up by Retrospect; can be restored based on the information saved in the.RBC backup catalog file. Retrospect was previously developed by Dantz software. The program is now owned and distributed by EMC Insignia. Windows EMC Insignia Retrospect Mac EMC Insignia Retrospect.",
    "Windows Microsoft Windows Installer Included with OS. Windows Executed on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. Mac Executed on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. Linux Executed on the EV3 Intelligent Brick. Windows Stellar Insta Backup Gold. Windows CELADE REDATAM. Windows EMC Insignia Retrospect. Mac EMC Insignia Retrospect.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".^^^",
    "Pervasive.SQL Database File",
    "2.5",
    "Database file used by Pervasive.SQL database software; based on the Btrieve transactional database format; created by the database engine when the database is placed in Continuous Operations mode. The Pervasive.SQL program was renamed Pervasive PSQL starting with version 9. Windows Pervasive PSQL.",
    "Windows Pervasive PSQL.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".FP5",
    "FileMaker Pro 5 Database",
    "2.4",
    "An FP5 file is a database created by FileMaker Pro 5 or 6. It contains one or more data tables, which may contain a record of a businesss inventory, contacts, personnel, or projects. The FP5 format replaced the.FP4 format and was itself replaced by the.FP7 format. Businesses use FileMaker Pro to input, track, and manage critical business data. Since its initial release in 1990, the program has had many versions. FileMaker Inc. released FileMaker Pro 5 in 1999 and FileMaker Pro 6 in 2002. Versions 5 and 6 of FileMaker Pro save users databases as FP5 files. These files contain one or more data tables, which users often view in spreadsheet form. For example, a user might open an FP5 file that contains a record of their businesss inventory, to note how many of a particular item they have on hand or from which vendor they purchase the item. NOTE: FileMaker Inc. was previously known as Claris. The company changed its name back to Claris in 2020. You can open an FP5 file with FileMaker Pro (Windows, Mac) versions 5 through 11. To open an FP5 file with a more recent version of FileMaker Pro, you must first convert the file to the current FileMaker Pro database format. For example, to open an FP5 file with FileMaker Pro 12, you must: Open the file with FileMaker Pro 11 to convert it to the.FP7 format. Open the converted FP7 file with FileMaker Pro 12 or a later version to convert it to the.FMP12 format. Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced. Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced.",
    "Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced. Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".FM5",
    "FileMaker 5 Database",
    "2.3",
    "Database created by FileMaker 5, a cross-platform database management program; may contain several tables, each with multiple fields. FileMaker 5 was the first major FileMaker release from FileMaker, Inc. The program was previously developed by Claris Corporation. FileMaker, Inc. is a wholly owned subsidiary of Apple, Inc. Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced. Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced.",
    "Mac FileMaker Pro Advanced. Windows FileMaker Pro Advanced.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".WRK",
    "SQL Server Log Shipping File",
    "2.3",
    "Project file created by Cakewalk, an audio production application; may split the production across multiple tracks and can include MIDI data, references to audio files, fader settings, tempos, audio effects, and other settings. The .wrk extension is used by older versions of Cakewalk. Newer versions use the.CWP extension. Windows Cakewalk SONAR X3. Database backup file created by SQL Server, a relational database management system (RDBMS); saves a backup of transaction logs while they are being copied to secondary storage; renamed to .trn when the backup is complete. The .wrk extension is assigned to the transaction log backup file temporarily during the backup operation. Therefore, if you see a WRK file that has not changed for a long period of time, it is possible that the backup operation failed. Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019.",
    "Windows Cakewalk SONAR X3. Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".BC3",
    "FIEBDC-3 Database File",
    "2.3",
    "A BC3 file is a database file saved in the FIEBDC-3 format, which is a Spanish standard construction database exchange format. It contains a collection of data records, which may include construction materials, cost of materials, and price of labor. BC3 files are typically utilized by construction professionals that plan and manage large-scale projects. These users can export, exchange, and import BC3 files between applications without losing data or converting the format. FIEBDC stands for Formato de Intercambio Estándar - Bases de Datos de Construcción, which translates to Standard Exchange Format - Construction Databases in English. It is an association that was established in July 1996 and oversees the FIEBDC construction database exchange format. NOTE: There are various versions of the FIEBDC-3 format that have been released throughout the years. Some versions include FIEBDC-3/2004, FIEBDC-3/2007, FIEBDC-3/2012, and FIEBDC-3/2016. You can open BC3 database files with a variety of construction and financial budgeting applications, such as Arktec Gest, Arktec Constructo, PREOC PREMETI, and CYPE Arquimedes. Windows CYPE Arquimedes. Arktec Gest. Arktec Constructo. PREOC PREMETI.",
    "Windows CYPE Arquimedes. Arktec Gest. Arktec Constructo. PREOC PREMETI.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".KNO",
    "SuperMemo Knowledge Collection",
    "2.0",
    "A KNO file is a data file created by DigIN, a program used for information management and knowledge discovery. It contains a break model, which classifies the information from a set of digital resources (documents, webpages, etc.) into a structure that allows patterns, relationships, and origins of data to be discovered. KNO files organize data by content, context, and structure, using a figure referred to as a Borromean ring. Break models organize data in such a way that information can be derived and extracted at any level of granularity that the user selects. Each break model can be analyzed at multiple levels of granularity and may be used to generate additional break models. NOTE: DigIN stands for Digital Integration and is a registered trademark of EvREsearch. DigIN is no longer available. Windows EvREsearch DigIN Kno-How Mac EvREsearch DigIN Kno-How. A KNO file is a knowledge collection created by SuperMemo, a memorization app for Windows. It contains a set of digital question-and-answer flashcards. Users can create, open, and back up KNO files in SuperMemo. KNO file open in SuperMemo World SuperMemo 18 SuperMemo is a knowledge memorization app published by SuperMemo World. In the past, the app was available primarily for Windows and supported generalized memorization, via question-and-answer flashcards. (Current versions of SuperMemo are available for Windows and mobile devices, and they specialize in language-learning courses that consist of vocabulary words and phrases.) These versions of SuperMemo save users flashcard collections as KNO files. To create a new KNO file, users select File → New collection. SuperMemo then creates the KNO file in its SuperMemo/​systems directory. In some versions of SuperMemo, users can also manually back up their KNO files to additional locations. You can open a KNO file in SuperMemo 18 (Windows) and some preceding versions of SuperMemo. Note that KNO files created by newer versions of SuperMemo may not open in older versions of the program (for example, a KNO file created by SuperMemo 18 may not open in SuperMemo 15). Windows SuperMemo World SuperMemo 18.",
    "Windows EvREsearch DigIN Kno-How. Mac EvREsearch DigIN Kno-How. Windows SuperMemo World SuperMemo 18.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".VPD",
    "VoxPro Database File",
    "2.0",
    "3D model file used by MikuMikuDance, a dance and rhythm synchronization game; saves bone positions for a characters model, which give it a pose; can be used in a series of poses that make up a dance animation (.VMD file). Windows MikuMikuDanceFree. A VPD file is a diagram created by the Diagram app module available with Visual Paradigm Online. It is saved in the Visual Paradigm Online Diagram (VPD) format and contains diagram elements, such as activities, shapes, images, graphics, and text. VPD file open in Visual Paradigm Online Visual Paradigm Online is the online counterpart to the desktop Visual Paradigm software. The tool allows you to design various artwork and documents, such as diagrams, posters, flyers, infographics, and greeting cards. After saving a design, you can re-open it with Visual Paradigm Online to continue modifying the design. When saving it, you can choose the location where to save it, including the Visual Paradigm online storage space, Google Drive, and local storage on your device. Visual Paradigm Online saves artwork in different formats depending on the app modules you are using. For example, if you create a design with the Graphic Design app module, Visual Paradigm Online saves it as an.ART file. However, if you create a diagram with the Diagram app module, Visual Paradigm Online saves it as a VPD file. How to create a VPD file To create a VPD file: Select File → Create New Design the diagram Select File → Save as.. Name the file and choose the save location (Google Drive or Device). You can open a VPD file with Visual Paradigm Online in a web browser. To open a VPD file, select File → Open. Web Visual Paradigm OnlineFree. Database file created by VoxPro, an audio recorder and editor; contains metadata about the contents of the folder its held in, which is retrieved and displayed by VoxPro. You can manually rebuild VPD files that may be out of sync with its folder contents by selecting File → Rebuild File Database. Also, VoxPro will identify any out-of-sync or deleted VPD files and update or recreate them automatically. NOTE: Audion Labs was acquired by Wheatstone Corporation. VP_EMap.vpd - Default database file contained in every folder of every user account in VoxPro. Windows Wheatstone VoxPro.",
    "Windows MikuMikuDance. Web Visual Paradigm Online. Windows Wheatstone VoxPro.",
    "Visual Paradigm Online can convert VPD files to the following image formats:.PDF - Portable Document Format.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.SVG - Scalable Vector Graphics File."],
    ["database_files",
    ".JTX",
    "ESE Transaction Log",
    "2.0",
    "Text file written using the JTX markup format, which is used for specifying the content of an HTML notebook; contains a table or contents and notebook page data; allows Jrju to build a hierarchical notebook with cross-references and HTML links. Jrju is distributed as Perl script that generates HTML files from a JTX text file. Windows Jrju Mac Jrju Linux Jrju. Log file generated by the Extensible Storage Engine (ESE), a database engine developed by Microsoft as part of the Windows API; stores records of changes to the database over time; used for backup and restore operations. The ESE technology was introduced with Windows 2000, but not all components of the API are available in all versions of Windows. ESE technology is used by programs such as Microsoft Exchange Server. Windows Microsoft Exchange Server. Document formatted in the XML Paper Specification (XPS) page description language, which was originally developed by Microsoft; defines page layout, appearance, and printing information; can be used for storing various personal and professional documents. By default, the .jtx extension is set as an XPS document file association in Windows 7, although the file extension is rarely used for XPS documents. The default extension for XPS documents is.XPS. Windows Microsoft XPS Viewer Included with OS.",
    "Windows Jrju. Mac Jrju. Linux Jrju. Windows Microsoft Exchange Server. Windows Microsoft XPS Viewer Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".XDB",
    "PowerDesigner Database Definition File",
    "2.0",
    "Virus database file used by Symantec AntiVirus, an antivirus program; contains updated virus definitions; used to distribute virus definitions over the Internet when new viruses are discovered. XDB files are commonly downloaded by a Symantec AntiVirus server within a company network and then distributed to client programs as.VDB files. Windows Symantec AntiVirus. Contains information about a PowerDesigner database (.PDM) file; may be the default definition file included with PowerDesigner or a custom file created by the user; required for a PowerDesigner database file to open correctly. Windows Sybase PowerDesigner.",
    "Windows Symantec AntiVirus. Windows Sybase PowerDesigner.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".PX",
    "PC-Axis Statistical Database",
    "2.0",
    "Image file saved by the Pixel image editor, a multi-platform image editing, photo retouching, graphics manipulation, and animation program; supports layers, paths, channels, masks, and selections; may also include adjustment and effects layer like a Photoshop (.PSD) document. Pixel image files can be saved in RGB, CMYK, grayscale, and CIE Lab modes, as well as the HDR (High Dynamic Range) format with 32-bit precision. The Pixel image editor was previously known as Pixel32. Windows Pixel image editor Mac Pixel image editor Linux Pixel image editor. A PX file is a statistical database crated for use with PxWin, a statistics analysis program created by Statistics Sweden. It contains a table-based dataset used to perform statistical analyses and calculations. PX files typically contain official government statistics. PX file open in Statistics Sweden PxWin Statistics Sweden is a Swedish government agency responsible for producing and disseminating official government statistics. One of the ways Statistics Sweden disseminates statistics is by providing datasets saved as PX files. These files can be opened and analyzed in PxWin, which is available for download from Statistics Swedens website. Each PX file consists of a set of key-value pairs that describe their datasets contents, followed by the dataset itself. In addition to being able to retrieve PX files from Statistics Sweden, users can create their own PX files from within PxWin, by clicking the Save button while viewing a database (or subset of a database). NOTE: Statistics Finland, Statistics Norway, Statistics Latvia, and Statistics Iceland also publish statistical databases saved in the PX format. You can open a PX file with Statistics Sweden PxWin (Windows). To do so, open PXWin and then drag and drop your PX file into the program. Windows Statistics Sweden PxWinFree.",
    "Windows Pixel image editor. Mac Pixel image editor. Linux Pixel image editor. Windows Statistics Sweden PxWin.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".KEXIC",
    "Kexi Database Connection File",
    "2.0",
    "File used by Kexi, a Linux relational database application which is sometimes used as an alternative to MS Access; saves connection data for connecting to a Kexi database (.KEXI file). KEXIC files differ from.KEXIS files. While a KEXIS file is used to connect to a specific database, a KEXIC file only saves connection parameters and does not include a specific database name. Therefore, KEXIC files are useful for saving connection settings and reusing them with multiple databases. Linux KexiFree.",
    "Linux Kexi.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ROD",
    "Ancestry Genealogical Database File",
    "2.0",
    "Database file used by RIB office, a project management application for planners and engineers in building construction, civil engineering, and road construction; stores all office data in the Progress ObjectStore database format; used as the backend format for saving RIB office data. ROD files can contain information such as time management data, drawings, employee information, contacts, contract data, and invoices. NOTE: RIB office is no longer available. Windows RIB office. Report design created with Actuate software, such as Actuate e.Report Designer; includes form layouts, fields, forms, and other information; used for customizing the output of reports generated with Actuate software. Executable reports are saved as.ROX files. Windows Actuate e.Report Designer. Database used by Ancestry, a program used to keep track of genealogical information; contains data about a users genealogical line, which includes family names, relationships, birth dates, photos, and anniversaries. Ancestry, which was originally named Rodokmen, is designed to help you organize your genealogical information and generate family trees. The ROD file is used to store and transfer your genealogical information. NOTE: The ROD file extension was replaced by the.RODX file extension, which was then replaced by the.RODZ extension. Windows Nethar Ancestry.",
    "Windows RIB office. Windows Actuate e.Report Designer. Windows Nethar Ancestry.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".ODLSENT",
    "Sent OneDrive Event Log",
    "2.0",
    "An ODLSENT file is a OneDrive event log (.ODL file) that has been sent to Microsoft. It contains a list of events that occurred while a user was using OneDrive. Microsoft uses the information ODLSENT files contain to troubleshoot synchronization issues caused by editing files offline in the desktop version of OneDrive. Microsoft OneDrive is a file hosting and sharing app that individuals and organizations use to store and share files. Primarily, users access OneDrive via a web browser. However, users can also install a desktop version of OneDrive, allowing them to access and edit their files offline. Offline changes a user makes in the desktop version of OneDrive are synced to their OneDrive account, and thus the web version of OneDrive, the next time they connect to the Internet. The desktop versions of OneDrive store a record of a users actions in an ODL file. Microsoft can use these files to troubleshoot synchronization issues with a users OneDrive account. After an ODL file has been sent to Microsoft, the files extension is changed to.odlsent, to denote that Microsoft has received the log the file contains. While ODLSENT files are not meant to be opened, you can view their contents with GitHub user ydkhatris OneDrive Log ODL Reader (multiplatform). Windows Microsoft OneDrive. OneDrive Log ODL Reader. Mac Microsoft OneDrive. OneDrive Log ODL ReaderFree.",
    "Windows Microsoft OneDrive. OneDrive Log ODL Reader. Mac Microsoft OneDrive. OneDrive Log ODL Reader.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".FKR",
    "Free Keylogger Report",
    "2.0",
    "An FKR file is a report created by IwantSoft FKL, a Windows keylogger and activity monitoring application. It contains a log of the actions a user performed on their computer during a monitored timeframe. For example, an FKR file lists the applications a user opened, the keys they pressed, and the websites they visited. FKR file open in IwantSoft FKL Businesses use IwantSoft FKL to monitor their employees PC usage. Periodically, FKL sends reports of users activities to an administrator via email, FTP, a local network, or Dropbox. These reports are saved as FKR files. Administrators can open FKR files in FKLs Report Viewer to view the information they contain. The reports Log section shows all the activities a user performed, divided into categories. By default, this information is listed chronologically. The reports Analytics section shows bar graphs of a users application and website usage. You can open an FKR file with IwantSoft FKL (Windows). To do so, open FKL and click the Import Reports button. Then, navigate to and open your FKR file. Windows IwantSoft FKL.",
    "Windows IwantSoft FKL.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".NS3",
    "Lotus Notes 3 Database",
    "2.0",
    "Database file created by Lotus Notes 3.x; contains contact information, a text notes, and calendar as well as other information; used to store structured information for collaboration with other users and for exchanging data back and forth; can be stored on a central server, which keeps users Notes databases up to date. Lotus Notes was acquired by IBM and is referred to as IBM Lotus Notes. Windows IBM Lotus Notes 2 or later Lotus Domino Mac IBM Lotus Notes 2 or later Lotus Domino.",
    "Windows IBM Lotus Notes 2 or later Lotus Domino. Mac IBM Lotus Notes 2 or later Lotus Domino.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".GWI",
    "GroupWise Database Shortcut File",
    "2.0",
    "File used by GroupWise, a collaboration program used in professional environments; contains a pointer to a GroupWise database object; may include a user ID, version, item type, message ID, and folder path. GWI files are used to save and share shortcuts to GroupWise database messages, records, and other information. NOTE: If the object that the GWI file refers to is removed from the GroupWise database, the GWI file is no longer useful. Windows Novell GroupWise. Mac Novell GroupWise. Linux Novell GroupWise.",
    "Windows Novell GroupWise. Mac Novell GroupWise. Linux Novell GroupWise.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".EDB",
    "Windows Search Index Database",
    "2.0",
    "An EDB file is a database created by Microsoft Exchange Server. It serves as the main repository for the mailbox data saved by Exchange. EDB files store both in-process and stored non-SMTP messages, formatted using a b-tree structure that includes a top-level node and many child nodes. Priv1.edb and Pub1.edb are the main EDB files used for the Exchange information store. They each have a corresponding.STM file that contains SMTP messages. Windows Microsoft Exchange Server. Stellar Repair for Exchange. Aryson EDB to PST Converter. EdbMails. Regain EDB to PST Converter. An EDB file is a database file created by the Windows Search feature included with Microsoft Windows. It contains indexed information about files that have been searched for in the Windows Search feature. EDB files allow the search feature to more quickly return results about files that have been previously searched. EDB files may grow large in size, up to several hundred gigabytes (GBs). You can delete the EDB file on your computer to free up space on your hard drive. However, doing this will erase the indexing You can find the EDB file in the following location: C:/​ProgramData/​Microsoft/​Search/​Data/​Applications/​Windows/​. Windows.edb - The name of the database that stores all the Windows Search indexed information. Windows Microsoft Windows.",
    "Windows Microsoft Exchange Server. Stellar Repair for Exchange. Aryson EDB to PST Converter. EdbMails. Regain EDB to PST Converter. Windows Microsoft Windows.",
    "?"],
    ["database_files",
    ".DCT",
    "FoxPro Database Memo",
    "2.0",
    "Data file used by various dictionary, translation, or word processing applications; typically contains a list of words and may also include definition or translation information; often used for spell-checking and may be available in different languages. Windows QuarkXPress. Various dictionary programs Mac QuarkXPress. Various dictionary programs. Variable codec audio format designed for dictation (recording human speech); includes a dictation header and can be encrypted, which may be required by medical confidentiality laws. Windows NCH Express Scribe. NCH Express Dictate. NCH Switch. NCH WavePad. Mac NCH Express Scribe. NCH Express Dictate. NCH Switch. NCH WavePad. Contains textual notes about a FoxPro database (.DBC file). Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Word dictionary used by AutoCAD, a CAD productivity application; stores a list of words used by the spell checker for identifying misspelled words; can be extended with custom user dictionaries, which are stored in.CUS files. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Cheats file used by DeSmuME, a Nintendo DS (NDS) emulator; contains cheats, such as infinite health, infinite armor, infinite ammo, extra lives, unlocked weapons, extra points, and secret levels, for NDS games that can be emulated by DeSmuME. Windows DeSmuME. Mac DeSmuME. Linux DeSmuMEFree. A DCT file is a video used by some Electronic Arts video games, including Need for Speed II. It contains a movie played within the game. DCT files are quite uncommon, so most popular media players cannot play them. DCT file open in VLC media player Need for Speed II was the second game released as part of Electronic Arts Need for Speed franchise. It allowed players to race a number of exotic cars on racetracks located around the world. EA released Need for Speed II in 1997 and has since released over 20 additional Need for Speed games. DCT movies feature real-life footage of cars that players can unlock within Need for Speed II. Players could watch these movies while learning more about the cars theyd acquired. Because DCT files are so uncommon, most popular media players cannot play them. However, you can play DCT files in VLC media player, and you can convert them to a more usable video format using FFmpeg. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpegFree.",
    "Windows QuarkXPress. Various dictionary programs. Mac QuarkXPress. Various dictionary programs. Windows NCH Express Scribe. NCH Express Dictate. NCH Switch. NCH WavePad. Mac NCH Express Scribe. NCH Express Dictate. NCH Switch. NCH WavePad. Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Windows DeSmuME. Mac DeSmuME. Linux DeSmuME. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg.",
    "?"],
